mza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When the application adds its data model to the existing PostgreSQL database, what should happen to any pre-existing database contents?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Preserve existing contents and add the application structures without discarding compatible data.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"When a ration defines ingredient proportions, what basis should the API use to calculate inventory consumption and ration cost?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat proportions as percentages of as-fed ingredient weight; use dry-matter values only for nutritional calculations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen when recording a feeding event whose ration requires more of an ingredient than is currently in inventory?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Reject the entire event without changing inventory or feed rollups.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the feed-to-gain metrics and projected ship date be represented when Days on Feed is zero or ADG is zero or negative?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Return the affected metrics and projected ship date as unavailable until the required positive denominator or gain exists.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all nine requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all nine requirements be approved as one run, or should the work be split or reduced?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should AC-5.1 provide an authenticated principal for protected list requests while keeping seeding disabled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Add a test-only account fixture, separate from demo seed data, and authenticate the protected-list requests with it.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement every HTTP operation in contracts/openapi.yaml with its declared methods, paths, parameters, schemas, security requirements, behavior, success and error statuses, and export file artifacts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Persist all application values read or changed by the API, including derived or cached values, in PostgreSQL through the existing App connection string, retain committed values across requests and restarts, and initialize required structures without changing or deleting pre-existing database contents.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true on a clean database, run App.Api/SeedData.cs to populate each application table with two or three believable rows based on contracts/openapi.yaml examples and expose those rows through list operations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, skip SeedData.Run and insert no demo rows, while serving contract operations, including protected lists on empty operational data authenticated through a separate test-only account fixture.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Expose backend API and documentation surfaces without product-facing web screens or frontend implementation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate ration ingredient consumption and cost from as-fed ingredient weights and use dry-matter values only for nutritional calculations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Atomically reject feeding event creation or correction that requires unavailable ingredient inventory with a 409 response and no changes to events, inventory, movements, or lot feed and cost rollups, including when requests run concurrently.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Apply successful feeding event corrections as replacements of the previous inventory and rollup effects, and reverse those effects when an event is voided.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Return affected ADG, feed-to-gain metrics, and projected ship dates as null when days on feed are zero, ADG is nonpositive, or no positive gain remains toward the target, as applicable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate applicable feed-to-gain metrics and projected ship dates from a positive gain rate when days on feed and gain are positive and the target weight has not been reached.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-2 has an anchor that doesn't match the code\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}